    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VUbU1ewTcBP1QZhAnejD1o)_\n\n- The scale prompts (`sp-litnotes-meta--read-scale`) used `completing-read` with require-match `t`, which refuses an empty answer, so a value was forced.\n- Now `(none)` is the first candidate and the default; choosing it (or an empty answer) returns nil and writes nothing.\n- Applies to relevance-factor, read-priority and the batch read-status prompt (all use `--read-scale`). The bib-project prompt already has a default; the other `completing-read` calls are not optional properties.\n- Prompts say \"(none) to skip\"; literate doc and ERT test updated. Checked the changed function in isolation on Emacs 29 (full suite needs the real config environment).\n- No CHANGELOG edit, per project rules.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiA1FVHMpuuWuB1rpe4)_",
    "changed_files": 3,
    "closed_at": "2026-11-09T22:53:34Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "OWNER",
            "body": "The `tangle` check failed because one docstring line in the doc (`sp-litnotes-meta.org`) differed from the module. My first commit changed it in the doc only by mistake. I pushed 048bd4c to fix it, and CI will re-run on it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
